      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَخْيوُلٌ</span></b> : see <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْيَلُ</span>. ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  Also A camel <i>lacerated
in his rump by a bird of the kind called</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَخْيَل</span>
<i>that has alighted upon it.</i> (TA.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And hence,
(assumed tropical:)  A man <i>whose reason has fled in consequence of
fright:</i> a sense in which it is used by the vulgar;
but correct. (TA.)

